{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Factor Inertia.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Factor Inertia.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"factor inertia factor inertia","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Factor Inertia.md","fileName":"Factor Inertia.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Factor Inertia","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 10:04\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Correspondence Analysis and Narrative Geometry]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Correspondence Analysis and Narrative Geometry","datasciencefoundations_geometry.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Factor Inertia.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Factor Inertia.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"factor inertia factor inertia","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Factor Inertia.md","fileName":"Factor Inertia.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Factor Inertia","heading":"Factor Inertia","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"In correspondence analysis, inertia is the mass-weighted squared distance of a point cloud from its center. Eigenvalue decomposition splits that total inertia among ordered factors, so the early factors capture larger portions of the table's variation.\n\nA two-dimensional plot is an approximation when it displays only two factors. The book repeatedly distinguishes visual interpretation from calculations in the full factor space: a low percentage of displayed inertia should make an analyst cautious about claims based solely on a planar diagram.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Correspondence Analysis and Narrative Geometry","datasciencefoundations_geometry.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Factor Inertia.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Factor Inertia.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName"